enges through a collaborative approach.", "EQUIPO TRANSDISCIPLINAR:A transdisciplinary team goes beyond traditional roles, allowing professionals to take on tasks from other disciplines to enhance patient care in dysphagia.", "ATENCIÓN INTEGRAL:Atención integral refers to the comprehensive care approach provided to patients with dysphagia, involving multiple disciplines.", "PROFESIONALES DE LA SALUD:\"PROFESIONALES DE LA SALUD\" refers to healthcare professionals who play a crucial role in providing medical services and support to patients. They are essential for the diagnosis and treatment of various conditions, including oropharyngeal dysphagia. These professionals are specifically involved in the treatment and rehabilitation of patients suffering from dysphagia, ensuring that individuals receive the necessary care and support to manage their condition effectively.", "ABORDAJE DE LA DISFAGIA:Abordaje de la disfagia refers to the strategies and methods used to treat and manage dysphagia.", "INTERVENCIÓN CONJUNTA:Intervención conjunta refers to the collaborative approach taken by various professionals in treating dysphagia.", "EVALUACIÓN DE PATOLOGÍAS:Evaluación de patologías refers to the assessment of medical conditions, including dysphagia, by a team of specialists.", "ENFOQUE MULTIDISCIPLINARIO:Enfoque multidisciplinario refers to the collaborative method involving multiple disciplines to address dysphagia treatment.", "VISIÓN COMPLETA:Visión completa refers to the comprehensive perspective gained through a multidisciplinary approach in dysphagia care.)<|COMPLETE|>", "NEUROLOGÍA:The entity \"NEUROLOGÍA\" refers to a specialized unit within a hospital dedicated to the diagnosis and treatment of disorders related to the nervous system. This department plays a crucial role in addressing various neurological conditions, including those that may lead to complications such as dysphagia, which is difficulty in swallowing. Through its comprehensive approach, the Neurology department aims to manage and treat the underlying causes of these disorders effectively.", "MEDICINA INTERNA:The \"MEDICINA INTERNA\" refers to the Internal Medicine department, which is a medical specialty focused on the diagnosis, treatment, and prevention of diseases in adults. This specialty encompasses a wide range of conditions affecting multiple systems of the body. The department is particularly noted for its role in managing patients with dysphagia, ensuring coordinated care for these individuals. Additionally, the Internal Medicine department emphasizes dietary considerations as part of its comprehensive care approach for adult patients. Overall, \"MEDICINA INTERNA\" plays a crucial role in providing thorough medical attention and support for various adult health issues.", "ONCOLOGÍA:The Oncology department addresses dysphagia in patients with cancer-related complications.", "ENDOCRINOLOGÍA Y NUTRICIÓN:\"ENDOCRINOLOGÍA Y NUTRICIÓN\" is a specialized field of medicine that focuses on hormonal and nutritional health. It encompasses both clinical practice and research, as evidenced by the existence of a scientific journal dedicated to this discipline. The journal, also named \"Endocrinología y Nutrición,\" serves as a platform for disseminating research findings related to endocrinology and nutrition. \n\nIn clinical settings, the Endocrinology and Nutrition department plays a crucial role in patient care, particularly for individuals with diabetes and those requiring nutritional support, such as dysphagia patients. This department is where patients are referred for evaluation after experiencing significant weight loss, highlighting its importance in managing various health concerns related to nutrition and hormonal balance.\n\nMartín López de la Torre Casares is noted for his specialization in this field, contributing to both the clinical and editorial aspects of endocrinology and nutrition. As an associate editor of the journal, he is involved in advancing knowledge and research in this vital area of healthcare.", "LOGOPEDAS:Logopedas are professionals who specialize in the evaluation and treatment of swallowing disorders, particularly in patients with dysphagia. They play a crucial role in assessing deglutition and the risk of aspiration in individuals receiving enteral nutrition. In both the United States and Europe, logopedas are primarily responsible for the care of patients with dysphagia, ensuring that these individuals receive appropriate interventions to manage their swallowing difficulties effectively.", "UNCYD:The Unidad de Nutrición Clínica y Dietética (UNCyD) is a clinical nutrition unit dedicated to conducting nutritional assessments and screenings, particularly for patients over the age of 65. It operates within a team-oriented framework, offering nutritional support tailored to individuals with special needs. UNCyD focuses on the management of clinical nutrition and dietary practices to enhance patient care and well-being."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}